WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.670
-Welcome, welcome, welcome,
welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.170
Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:06.940
Thank you for being here.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.274
Well, guys, today,

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:10.710
a group of leading U.S.
and international scientists

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.578
announced new data that shows

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:16.616
COVID booster shots are
not appropriate at this time.

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:18.651
[ Audience ohs ]

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:19.819
Yeah, and then scientists saw

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:21.854
100 sold-out football stadiums
this weekend

00:00:21.854 --> 00:00:24.857
and were like, "Hold that
thought. Hold on a second."

00:00:24.857 --> 00:00:25.958
Yep, they said

00:00:25.958 --> 00:00:27.726
they're absolutely sure
of their findings

00:00:27.726 --> 00:00:29.762
and look forward
to changing them next week.

00:00:29.762 --> 00:00:31.330
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:33.265
It seems like these scientists
can't make up their mind.

00:00:33.265 --> 00:00:34.834
I say we just
split the difference

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:37.103
and just start
microdosing Pfizer.

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:38.371
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.206
Meanwhile,
as if the Delta variant

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:41.507
isn't causing enough problems,

00:00:41.507 --> 00:00:44.477
apparently, it's now led
to a shortage of printing paper.

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:46.179
-Oh.
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:48.314
-This is a big deal.
If this is true,

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:50.984
my dad will have no way
to print out his e-mails.

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:53.520
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.487 --> 00:00:56.789
"Hold on a second, Jimmy.

00:00:56.789 --> 00:01:00.426
Let me read what you wrote.
Hold on a second."

00:01:00.426 --> 00:01:03.096
The paper shortage is so bad,
book sellers are worried

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:06.565
there might not be enough paper
to print books.

00:01:06.565 --> 00:01:07.900
See, this is what happens

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.169
when one out of three people
write a Trump tell-all.

00:01:10.169 --> 00:01:11.437
That's what I've been saying.

00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:13.473
Hey, everyone's got to stop
with the tell-alls.

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:15.975
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:19.011
Well, this is fun. Ahead of
the newest "James Bond" film,

00:01:19.011 --> 00:01:21.180
one company
is looking to hire someone

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:23.749
to be an official
martini tester.

00:01:23.749 --> 00:01:26.219
-Whoo!
-Whoo!

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:27.453
-That sounds like a job

00:01:27.453 --> 00:01:29.189
a contestant on
"The Bachelorette" would have.

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:31.090
Like, "Hi. My name's Todd B.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:32.825
I'm an official martini tester."

00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:34.527
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:35.828
This wasn't good. Yesterday

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:39.231
at the Washington Football
Team's season opener --

00:01:39.231 --> 00:01:41.267
That's the name.
They're sticking with that name.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.402
The Washington
Football Team, yeah.

00:01:43.402 --> 00:01:45.705
At the Washington
Football Team's season opener,

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:49.074
a pipe at the stadium burst
over a group of fans,

00:01:49.074 --> 00:01:51.110
and some people said
it might have been sewage.

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:54.047
[ Audience groans ]
I don't know. Take a look.

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:57.716
-That's sewage.
-Ah.

00:01:57.716 --> 00:02:00.987
-That's sewage?

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:03.590
-Well, that's a good omen
for the season, you know?

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:06.258
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.258 --> 00:02:08.061
Washington is still looking
for a team name,

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:10.062
and it's too bad the Browns
is already taken.

00:02:10.062 --> 00:02:13.066
-Hey! Oh, oh!

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:15.734
Oh! Oh, hey!

00:02:15.734 --> 00:02:18.004
-But the fans, the fans
embraced it all day long.

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:21.040
They were chanting, "We're
number one and number two!"

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.809
We're number --"
Ah, there you go.

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:24.744
[ Applause ]

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:28.281
This is interesting. I read
that emojis may be the new way

00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:31.718
patients communicate
with their doctor.

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:33.552
I don't know. Do you really
want to receive bad news

00:02:33.552 --> 00:02:35.588
from your doctor by getting
the thumbs-down emoji?

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:38.390
I -- Sounds a little strange,

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:40.359
but instead of having to explain
something embarrassing,

00:02:40.359 --> 00:02:42.594
you could just send this.

00:02:42.594 --> 00:02:46.265
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:46.265 --> 00:02:47.834
-Ow!

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:53.773
-Well, get this.
A team of scientists

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:56.309
are potty-training cows

00:02:56.309 --> 00:03:00.412
in an effort to reduce the
emissions caused by their waste.

00:03:00.412 --> 00:03:02.614
Which means stores are going
to start charging extra

00:03:02.614 --> 00:03:05.518
for grass-fed, free-range,
potty-trained beef.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:06.652
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.652 --> 00:03:07.720
What a job. Every night,

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.021
the scientists come home
smelling like

00:03:09.021 --> 00:03:11.457
they just left the Washington
Football Team's stadium,

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:13.559
you know?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:16.596
And, finally, last night,
Jon Stewart and Pete Davidson

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:19.499
put on a big benefit show
at Madison Square Garden

00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:22.601
called "NYC Still Rising
After 20 Years."

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:24.203
And it was --

00:03:24.203 --> 00:03:26.038
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:26.038 --> 00:03:29.275
Good for them.

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:30.810
It was great.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:33.078
I was there,
and I wrote a song for it,

00:03:33.078 --> 00:03:35.314
and I'd like to play it for you
right now, if you don't mind.

00:03:35.314 --> 00:03:37.049
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:37.049 --> 00:03:38.551
Thank you, bud.

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.119
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:41.955
Thank you.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.492
Madison Square Garden,
how you guys doing?

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:49.162
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:52.731 --> 00:03:54.434
My name is Jimmy Fallon.
I'm a New Yorker,

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:56.836
and I got a little song for you.

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:59.005
[ Guitar playing ]

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:01.040
♪♪

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:05.211
♪ I don't care
if you're Moderna or Pfizer ♪

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:08.914
♪ Johnson &amp; Johnson
or horse tranquilizer ♪

00:04:08.914 --> 00:04:11.350
♪ I know ♪

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:14.153
♪ New York's coming back ♪

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:16.322
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:18.825
♪♪

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:23.396
♪ We got the Rangers, Yankees,
Mets, Knicks, and Nets ♪

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:27.200
♪ We cheer for the Giants
and we pray for the Jets ♪

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.968
♪ Well, I know ♪

00:04:29.968 --> 00:04:32.638
♪ New York's coming back ♪

00:04:32.638 --> 00:04:36.575
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:36.575 --> 00:04:40.780
♪ We're already complaining
about the cold ♪

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:46.585
♪ We all hate Bill de Blasio,
and I know ♪

00:04:46.585 --> 00:04:49.455
♪ New York's coming back ♪

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:51.824
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:51.824 --> 00:04:56.362
♪ We got the NYPD and the FDNY ♪

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:58.764
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:58.764 --> 00:05:00.866
♪ When I tried out, they said ♪

00:05:00.866 --> 00:05:03.802
"You seem more like
a post office guy."

00:05:03.802 --> 00:05:06.271
♪ So I know ♪

00:05:06.271 --> 00:05:09.475
♪ New York's coming back ♪

00:05:09.475 --> 00:05:12.878
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:12.878 --> 00:05:15.815
♪ All the tourists
have returned ♪

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:20.519
♪ Doing what they do ♪

00:05:20.519 --> 00:05:23.723
♪ Walking slowly
down the sidewalk ♪

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:27.893
♪ Right in front of you ♪

00:05:27.893 --> 00:05:31.263
♪ Even though
some of the seats are wet ♪

00:05:31.263 --> 00:05:35.200
♪ The subway is still packed ♪

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:39.839
♪ I know New York City's
coming back ♪

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:43.042
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:46.678
♪♪

00:05:46.678 --> 00:05:50.383
♪ New York is back,
you can't keep us down ♪

00:05:50.383 --> 00:05:52.618
♪ You can travel the world ♪

00:05:52.618 --> 00:05:55.187
But there's no place
like this town.

00:05:55.187 --> 00:05:56.789
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:56.789 --> 00:06:02.328
♪ So I know
New York City's back ♪

00:06:02.328 --> 00:06:05.264
♪♪

00:06:05.264 --> 00:06:11.337
♪ I know New York City's
coming back ♪

00:06:11.337 --> 00:06:13.905
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:13.905 --> 00:06:15.208
I love you, New York!

